WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.120
now as 2021 draws to a close i think we're&nbsp;
all getting ready for Christmas but i want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.720
to take a bit of an opportunity just to talk&nbsp;
through some of the highlights of this year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.840
and some of the activities and actions that&nbsp;
we've been taking as a council to support our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.520
residents and businesses now back in January we&nbsp;
announced that Sharley park leisure center and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.400
the sports hall there was going to be used as&nbsp;
part of the vaccination rollout for coronavirus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.960
and over the course of the year over the following&nbsp;
months we supported the NHS to deliver 60,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.760
vaccinations from that centre and i'm really&nbsp;
pleased that the North East Derbyshire District&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:41.200
council has been recognised for its contribution&nbsp;
to that fantastic vaccine rollout over the course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.880
of the year and then in February we announced&nbsp;
that we were investing in our environmental health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.080
service both in terms of helping with the public&nbsp;
health response to Covid but also to help us deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.040
with issues like fly tipping and environmental&nbsp;
crime and that's been a fantastic achievement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.760
to be able to expand that service and really get&nbsp;
into some of those difficult issues that we face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.720
in our rural districts in March we&nbsp;
have an absolutely fantastic month&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:13.120
in terms of government funding for this district&nbsp;
firstly we had the amazing announcement of 24.1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.160
million pounds for clay cross as part of the Clay&nbsp;
Cross town deal then we also found out we'd have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.320
been awarded 1.6 million pounds which we've topped&nbsp;
up with council the council's own funding to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.360
us deliver external wall insulation to over 400&nbsp;
properties around the district and particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.880
those hard to heat homes and then finally we&nbsp;
also received a one million pound grant from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.560
government to help us improve Eckington leisure&nbsp;
centre and make it one of the most greenest and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.520
most environmentally friendly leisure centres in&nbsp;
the whole of the region and that works almost due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:52.080
for completion and hopefully will be reopened as&nbsp;
a pool very very soon now in April we elected our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:58.960
35th chairman of the council Councillor Martin&nbsp;
Thacker and he launched his fundraising campaign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.400
for Ashgate hospicecare and since then he's done&nbsp;
an absolute smattering of events throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:10.160
year and some fantastic fundraising activities&nbsp;
to raise vital funds for Ashgate hospicecare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.320
now in may we held some a very difficult set&nbsp;
of elections because of code restrictions but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:22.400
fortunately they ran very very smoothly and we had&nbsp;
lots of positive feedback from residents about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.120
whole process of voting and all the mitigations&nbsp;
that we put in place to help make voting and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.960
that key part of being a democratic country&nbsp;
possible during the month of May and then in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.400
June we worked with the government to support the&nbsp;
'kickstart scheme' to help give more young people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.960
really valuable experience in work now in July we&nbsp;
signed the contract with Killamarsh parish council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:50.480
as part of our 1.9 million takeover and&nbsp;
refurbishment of the sports centre there now works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.360
already started and i'm really looking forward to&nbsp;
that that centre reopening in the next few months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.120
and then also in the summer we had some&nbsp;
fantastic awards for some of our services&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.320
our health and safety team were awarded the&nbsp;
gold rosper award and our street scene team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.680
were also awarded an APSE award for excellent&nbsp;
services so well done to both of those teams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.120
now in September we launched together with&nbsp;
the other districts and county councils across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:23.280
Derbyshire we launched our 'Vision Derbyshire&nbsp;
'business grants and advice to businesses now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:29.920
in October we became the first council&nbsp;
in Derbyshire to implement mandatory CCTV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.720
for taxis and private hire vehicles now&nbsp;
we think that will help make both the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.080
passengers and the drivers themselves safer and&nbsp;
we're really proud to have been the first council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.400
to have done that and also throughout October we&nbsp;
did a series of meet the council events and also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.680
our armed forces covenant event to celebrate the&nbsp;
fantastic work of the armed forces in November we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:58.560
delivered a jobs fair in Clay Cross to help local&nbsp;
people find local jobs and also our environmental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:05.040
health team and did a fantastic job in seizing&nbsp;
and crushing a vehicle that was known to have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:12.240
involved in fly tipping in this area well done to&nbsp;
them and this month December we've announced our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.800
involvement in the queen's green canopy scheme&nbsp;
which involves planting trees to help mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.280
the queen's platinum jubilee next year we're&nbsp;
really excited to be part of this amazing project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.800
and that's just to name a few there's plenty more&nbsp;
on our website and on our social media channels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.360
so please do check them out and find out more&nbsp;
about the fantastic things that we've been we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.480
been doing throughout this year now I know that&nbsp;
this time at the moment is a particularly anxious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:44.160
time for some people with the concerns around the&nbsp;
omicron variant and the government's move to plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:50.000
b but i think it's absolutely vital that we all&nbsp;
continue to work together to follow the guidance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.400
and follow those restrictions where necessary and&nbsp;
also make sure that we all get our vaccinations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.360
done and go for our boosters when we're called&nbsp;
to do so we can continue to work together and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:07.840
i'm sure we can defeat the virus and continue to&nbsp;
enjoy a good Christmas together all the same and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:13.920
i hope everyone has a fantastic Christmas and a&nbsp;
very happy new year and look forward to 2022 when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.080
i'm sure there's a lot more things we can&nbsp;
do as a council working with our residents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.840
and our businesses and our community groups&nbsp;
and parish councils thank you very much.

